          <details>
            <summary>Participation expectations <span class="hint">(expand)</span></summary>
            <p>
              Participation includes engaging in discussion, answering questions, asking timely questions, and completing homework.
              Students must log into Blackboard weekly and complete all assignments.
            </p>
            <p class="muted">
              After two weeks of inactivity (not logging into Blackboard and completing assignments), students will not be able to pass the course,
              with exceptions per SKYCTC policy and the Healthy at SKYCTC initiative.
            </p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>Extra credit, late work, and make-up work <span class="hint">(expand)</span></summary>
            <ul>
              <li>Extra credit is not offered.</li>
              <li>Late/make-up work is not accepted except in circumstances outlined by SKYCTC policies and the Healthy at SKYCTC initiative.</li>
            </ul>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>Instructor withdrawal guidelines <span class="hint">(expand)</span></summary>
            <p>
              Students may withdraw themselves until the midpoint. After midpoint, withdrawal requires instructor approval.
              To request approval, students should contact the instructor to discuss progress and options; an email or conversation is required
              before approval (exceptions include certain Starfish flags).
            </p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>Professional conduct and disruptive behavior <span class="hint">(expand)</span></summary>
            <p>
              Actions that prevent teaching or learning are disruptive and not acceptable in academic or workplace settings.
              Derogatory, disrespectful, rude, argumentative, or hateful comments/actions toward the instructor or other students will not be tolerated,
              including discussion board posts. Code of Conduct infractions are handled with progressive discipline as described in the Code.
            </p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>Original work policy <span class="hint">(expand)</span></summary>
            <p>
              All work should be original and not previously submitted or published in another course or location.
              If you have questions, contact the instructor before completing the task/assignment.
            </p>
          </details>
